[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a bounded change: it modifies the existing activity page. I'll show you a short design in chat and won't write
  a spec file.

  The first question is where the filters go on the page, which is easier to see than describe. I've opened a browser
  tab with sketches at:
  [94m]8;id=1ljb2s5;http://localhost:52458/?key=a563f987546ad6583b242d03ca67fd9e2f0619e2e553e4ff2c3d08756508faed\http://localhost:52458/?key=a563f987546ad6583b242d03ca67fd9e2f0619e2e553e4ff2c3d08756508faed[39m]8;;\
  The sketches use a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather keep this in the terminal.

  The tab has three wireframes:
  - [1mA. Inline row above the table:[0m the controls are always visible and wrap into a stack on narrow screens. This needs
    the least code.
  - [1mB. Panel beside the table:[0m this leaves room for more filters later, but it narrows a six-column table and needs its
    own rules for small screens.
  - [1mC. Filter button with a popover and removable tags:[0m this is the most compact, but it takes an extra click to reach
    the controls and needs the most JavaScript and keyboard-focus handling.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It's the smallest change, it's the simplest to make work on a 320px screen and with a keyboard, and a
  "Sign-in failed" filter stays visible without opening anything. Which filters to offer is a separate question I'll ask
  next. The controls in the sketches are placeholders.

  Take a look and tell me what you think here. You can also click an option in the browser.

  Two other things I found:
  - [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m doesn't link a shared token stylesheet; it only loads [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m. I'll need to check where the
    guideline tokens are defined before writing any styles.
  - [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m. The sketches are saved there, so you may want to add it. I haven't changed
    [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m.

